AI Company Adoption Dataset

The AI Company adoption dataset, its a global, multi-year dataset recording Artificial Intelligence 
(AI) adoption trends, and business outcomes across thousands of organizational survey responses.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dataset Overview

The dataset tracks longitudinal metrics across enterprise and startup environments to evaluate
how organizations integrate AI technologies, manage risk, and observe returns on investment.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Data Schema & Field Definitions

The dataset consists of 43 feature columns categorized into five functional domains:

1. Organizational Profile

response_id: Unique identifier for each survey entry (1–150,000).

company_id: Unique identifier for the organization.

survey_year / quarter: Temporal tracking (2023–2026, Q1–Q4).

country / region: Geographic location of the reporting entity.

industry: Primary operating sector.

company_size: Size tier (Startup, SME, Enterprise).

num_employees: Total headcount.

annual_revenue_usd_millions: Annual revenue in USD ($M).

company_founding_year / company_age / company_age_group: Firm tenure metrics.


2. AI Deployment & Usage
  
ai_adoption_rate: Percentage of internal processes leveraging AI tools.

ai_adoption_stage: Current lifecycle phase (Evaluation, Pilot, Operational, Enterprise-Wide).

years_using_ai: Cumulative years of AI implementation.

ai_primary_tool: Core platform used (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, GitHub Copilot, Custom Internal AI, Other).

num_ai_tools_used: Number of distinct AI tools deployed.

ai_use_case: Primary application area (e.g., Customer Support, Software Development, HR Automation).

ai_projects_active: Count of active AI initiatives.

ai_training_hours: Hours of AI training provided per employee per year.


3. Investment & Governance
ai_budget_percentage: Proportion of overall IT budget allocated to AI.

ai_maturity_score: Standardized rating of organizational AI readiness (0–100).

ai_failure_rate: Rate of non-deployable or abandoned AI projects.

ai_investment_per_employee: Direct investment per worker ($ USD).

regulatory_compliance_score: Rating for compliance adherence.

data_privacy_level: Assessment level (Low, Medium, High, Strict).

ai_ethics_committee: Indicator of formal AI governance oversight (Yes / No).

ai_risk_management_score: Rating of AI-specific risk mitigation practices.

4. Workforce & Operational Impact
remote_work_percentage: Share of workforce operating remotely.

employee_satisfaction_score: Internal sentiment index (1.0–10.0 scale).

task_automation_rate: Percentage of routine tasks automated.

time_saved_per_week: Hours saved per employee per week.

productivity_change_percent: Observed net productivity delta (%).

jobs_displaced: Number of roles eliminated due to AI integration.

jobs_created: New roles created due to AI adoption.

reskilled_employees: Number of employees reskilled for AI workflows.

5. Business & Financial Performance
revenue_growth_percent: Year-over-year revenue growth (%).

cost_reduction_percent: Operational expense reduction (%).

innovation_score: Measured rate of product/service innovation.

customer_satisfaction: External satisfaction metric (1.0–10.0 scale).

survey_source / data_collection_method: Provenance and capture methodology.

